            "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n\n   The single user message was a `/goal` slash command: **\"Complete the task defined in @cfd_solver_agentic_benchmark/ .\"** \u2014 installed as a session-scoped Stop hook, meaning work must continue until the benchmark task is genuinely complete.\n\n   The benchmark (`/workspace/cfd_solver_agentic_benchmark/`) requires building, from scratch, a 2-D unstructured finite-volume compressible Navier\u2013Stokes solver and delivering a complete, validated, documented submission:\n   - **C++17 or newer core**; **MPI domain decomposition with halo/ghost exchange is mandatory**; Python allowed only for wrappers/preprocessing/plotting/report.\n   - Implementation must live in `<workspace>/solver/` (the benchmark repo is **read-only input** \u2014 no commits inside it, no modification of its tracked files); commit on a **new named branch** of the parent repo.\n   - **METIS/ParMETIS** partitioning of the cell adjacency graph; no full-mesh or full-state replication during iterations; neighbour-scoped halo exchange (no `MPI_Allgather` of state); global reductions for residuals/forces.\n   - Physics: conservative 2-D compressible NS, calorically perfect gas, Newtonian stress + Fourier heat flux, farfield / slip wall / no-slip adiabatic wall BCs, \u03bc = \u03c1\u221eU\u221eL_ref/Re.\n   - Numerics: cell-centred FV, \u22652nd-order piecewise-linear reconstruction **active in production**, mandatory shock limiter (Barth minimum), positivity preservation, approximate Riemann flux (Rusanov minimum), implicit main path with LU-SGS/SGS/Jacobi inner iterations, **true two-level dual-time BDF2/trapezoidal** for the Re 200 cylinder.\n   - Run **all 8 cases** to convergence or statistical periodicity; np=8 on \u22651 NACA and \u22651 cylinder case plus a rank-count comparison.\n   - Produce the exact `OUTPUT_CONTRACT.md` file layout per case, plus `report"
